 This install applies to "Prince of Persia 2: The Shadow and the Flame"
 (Macintosh version), copyright 1993, 1994 Jordan Mechner / Broderbund.
 Amiga port by Vesa Halttunen (Vesuri).

 Requirements:
 -------------
 PAL AGA Amiga, 68030 or better, 2 MB Chip RAM and at least 8 MB Fast RAM.
 WHDLoad 18.0 or newer and Installer 43 or newer must be installed.
 WHDLoad and PRELOAD require memory in addition to the game's memory.
 The program can be quit by pressing F10 (Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 An A1200 Kickstart 3.1 image and its matching RTB must be installed in
 DEVS:Kickstarts as "kick40068.A1200" and "kick40068.A1200.RTB".
 Supply your own licensed Kickstart image. The RTB is available in
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on Aminet.

 Installation:
 -------------
 To install or reinstall the game data, download
 "Prince_Of_Persia2.SIT" from:

 https://www.macintoshrepository.org/download.php?id=4673

 Leave the downloaded file compressed. Run the Install icon and select the
 destination parent drawer. Allow at least 40 MB free,
 plus space to preserve an existing installation.

 If verified game data is already installed, choose Use existing or Reinstall.
 Only data installation asks for the downloaded archive. Both choices preserve
 saved games and preferences, and keep a backup of the previous installation.
 The executable, slave, icon and ReadMe are always reinstalled.

 Extraction can take several minutes. The installer verifies the data before
 replacing the installed files and removes its temporary files afterwards.

 Start the installed game using its PrinceOfPersia2 icon. PRELOAD is enabled
 by default; disable that Tooltype if there is insufficient memory to cache
 the files. No game data, Kickstart, Workbench or WHDLoad is included.

 Features:
 ---------
 - Original 512 x 384 graphics on a PAL hires interlaced display.
 - Music and sound effects through Paula.
 - Hard disk installation, save games and quit to Workbench.

 Controls:
 ---------
 Space starts play. Use the cursor keys to move, Shift for careful movement
 and grabbing, and Ctrl for sword actions.
 Amiga-N: new game       Amiga-E: end game       Amiga-Q: quit
 Amiga-O: load game      Amiga-S: save game      Amiga-P: pause
 Amiga-T: sound          Amiga-M: music          Amiga-R: restart
 Amiga-H: hall of fame   F10: quit WHDLoad

